# Record formats — recutils descriptors, versioned and stable (requirement 101).
# One record of each kind, as it appears in the stores both profiles use.

%rec: State
%doc: An actor's snapshot. Git-only: actors/<kind>/<id>/state.rec. Tracker: the issue body's fenced block, validated by seq.
%key: id
%mandatory: id kind version state seq epoch

id: unit/atlas/b-0142/u-3
kind: unit
version: 1
state: building
seq: 7
epoch: 3
type: default
type-version: 3
bolt: bolt/atlas/b-0142
deps:
claims: providers/one-writer@3
approved-by: word/discord-1423581234567890
consumed: planning/atlas:12 bolt/atlas/b-0142:9
reason: decided approve yes
evidence: point=2026-09-04T07:41:02Z decisions/unit/atlas/b-0142/u-3/approve=answered

%rec: Message
%doc: One mailbox entry. Git-only: actors/<target>/mailbox/<id>.rec, deleted by the consuming commit. Tracker: a comment `kind: message` on the target's issue.
%key: id
%mandatory: id sender seq kind

id: bolt/atlas/b-0142/9/1
sender: bolt/atlas/b-0142
seq: 9
kind: unit.approved
to: unit/atlas/b-0142/u-3
payload: {"unit":"unit/atlas/b-0142/u-3"}
at: 2026-09-04T07:41:02Z

%rec: Lease
%doc: Actor ownership by a host. Renewal is the host's heartbeat, not a change here.
%key: actor
%mandatory: actor holder epoch taken

actor: bolt/atlas/b-0142
holder: host/studio
epoch: 3
taken: 2026-09-04T07:41:05Z

%rec: Word
%doc: One word as it arrived. Git-only: words/<id>.rec written by the word writer. Tracker: a comment the bot or the operator wrote.
%key: id
%mandatory: id decision answer who when source

id: word/discord-1423581234567890
decision: decision/unit/atlas/b-0142/u-3/approve
rendering: 2026-09-04T07:40:00Z
row: 2
answer: yes
text:
who: chuck
when: 2026-09-04T07:40:41Z
source: discord message 1423581234567890 in #flywheel

%rec: Verdict
%doc: The ledger. ledger/<repo>.rec, append-only; latest per claim wins.
%key: id
%mandatory: id repo claim claim-version revision verdict evidence judged-by date

id: verdict/atlas/providers/one-writer/3/2026-09-04T09:12:44Z
repo: atlas
claim: providers/one-writer
claim-version: 3
revision: 8f3c2a1
verdict: satisfied
evidence: openspec/specs/status-writer/spec.md#one-writer
judged-by: session/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/review-1-reviewer
date: 2026-09-04T09:12:44Z
effect: wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/14/1

%rec: Capture
%doc: One source event. captures/<key>.rec; the key makes a second import the same capture (requirement 98, S22).
%key: key
%mandatory: key source at captured-by raw

key: meeting/2026-09-02/atlas-sync
source: meeting
at: 2026-09-02T15:00:00Z
captured-by: chuck
raw: file:///Volumes/notes/transcripts/2026-09-02-atlas-sync.txt
signals: 20

%rec: Signal
%doc: Immutable once written (requirement 100). signals/<id>.rec.
%key: id
%mandatory: id capture kind asserted-by assertion excerpt position

id: signal/meeting-2026-09-02-atlas-sync/07
capture: meeting/2026-09-02/atlas-sync
kind: constraint
asserted-by: Dana
subject: providers rate-limits
assertion: The provider allows one writer per account, so retries must serialize.
excerpt: "…we only ever get one writer per account, retries pile up…"
position: 00:41:12
argues-with: providers/one-writer@3
event-date: 2026-09-02

%rec: Move
%doc: Curation's standing judgment on a signal; exactly one per signal (requirement 94). moves/<signal-id>.rec, replaced only by the operator's word.
%key: signal
%mandatory: signal move reason date by

signal: signal/meeting-2026-09-02-atlas-sync/07
move: challenge
target: providers/one-writer@3
reason: asserts the opposite of the claim's scenario 2
date: 2026-09-04T06:10:00Z
by: session/curation/org/41

%rec: Exit
%doc: What a session writes in its place: <place>/.flywheel/exits.rec, via `flywheel exit`, which validates against this descriptor. Terminal kinds: done, blocked, stalled. Non-terminal: finding, chore, signal.
%key: id
%mandatory: id kind at
%allowed: kind done blocked finding chore signal

id: exit/3
kind: finding
at: 2026-09-04T08:55:10Z
about: bolt/atlas/b-0142
text: The boundary claim providers/one-writer draws puts retries on the wrong side; a per-account queue would remove the race.

%rec: Claim
%doc: A fenced ```claim block inside its chapter; this is its parsed form in the generated claims index. The lock is the hash of the normalized block text; the archive step refuses a text change without a version move.
%key: name
%mandatory: name version scope lock scenarios chapter

name: providers/one-writer
version: 3
scope: capability:provider-client
lock: sha256:4be1…
scenarios: 2
chapter: src/providers/writes.md#one-writer

%rec: Dictation
%doc: The operator's own word with no row (requirement 11). dictations/<id>.rec, written by the word writer.
%key: id
%mandatory: id who when text target

id: dictation/discord-1423599999
who: chuck
when: 2026-09-05T10:02:00Z
text: unit on plan-rows: status page drops the host column when narrow
target: bolt/atlas/b-0142
applied: unit/atlas/b-0142/u-5

%rec: Effect
%doc: One outbox entry: a world effect the transition write recorded and the world may not yet show. Git-only: actors/<kind>/<id>/outbox.rec, the entry removed by the tick that finds the result in the world. Tracker: in the transition comment; listed as performed in the next.
%key: id
%mandatory: id name args

id: session/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/build-1-builder/2/1
name: session.start
args: {"session":"session/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/build-1-builder","place":"wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1","template":"build","instructions":"9c1e4f0"}
shows-as: session.process != absent

%rec: Note
%doc: Discussion about an object (requirement 131). Git-only: actors/<kind>/<id>/notes/<seq>.md with this header. Tracker: a comment `kind: note`.
%key: id
%mandatory: id actor who at

id: note/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/4
actor: wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1
who: session/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/build-1-builder
at: 2026-09-04T08:12:30Z
text: Two readings of providers/one-writer sc.2 — does "one writer" bound retries per account or per process? Exiting blocked.

%rec: Report
%doc: The machinery's own problems, never work (requirement 70). report/<host>.rec, append-only; the plan shows attention-class entries once.
%key: id
%mandatory: id host at severity reason

id: report/studio/2026-09-04T08:40:11Z/1
host: host/studio
at: 2026-09-04T08:40:11Z
severity: warn
reason: session attempted a line operation and was refused
evidence: refusal/wi/atlas/b-0142/u-3/1/2 hook=pre-push branch=feature/x
